<metadata><name>Salt Creek Falls trails (Diamond Creek Falls ski loop) from Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:292-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.611310" lon="-122.127552"><ele>1249.0</ele><name>Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 554578585); confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; book_elev_ft: 4080; quote: Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park ... At 4,080 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.610260" lon="-122.128680"><ele>1249.4</ele><name>Diamond Creek Falls trailhead, south of the Salt Creek bridge</name><desc>source: west end of USFS SNO-4376 / start of USFS SNO-3598 Diamond Creek Falls Loop XC; confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; quote: located southwest of the sno-park where a forest trail leads to the trail system</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.610080" lon="-122.129380"><ele>1251.4</ele><name>Start of the forest trail (SNO-3598 east end)</name><desc>source: last vertex of USFS SNO-3598 (60 m from its first vertex; the loop's ends do not join in EDW); confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; quote: a forest trail leads to the trail system</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.607260" lon="-122.135600"><ele>1311.6</ele><name>Forest trail meets the road (SNO-4378 start)</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-3598 vertex where SNO-4378 Diamond Creek Falls Road XC begins (OSM roads 5893-062 / 420 meet 90 m south); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 294; quote: A 3-mile trail system, primarily on roads</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.607868" lon="-122.142725"><ele>1304.8</ele><name>West end of the road part of the loop</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-3598 vertex where it leaves SNO-4378 to turn north; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 294; quote: primarily on roads</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.610260" lon="-122.128680"><ele>1249.4</ele><name>Diamond Creek Falls trailhead (loop closed)</name><desc>source: first vertex of USFS SNO-3598; confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; quote: a forest trail leads to the trail system</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.611310" lon="-122.127552"><ele>1249.0</ele><name>Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin; confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; book_elev_ft: 4080; quote: Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Salt Creek Falls trails (Diamond Creek Falls ski loop) from Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park -&gt; Diamond Creek Falls trailhead, south of the Salt Creek bridge: usfs-trail (high), 0.17 mi | 2. Diamond Creek Falls trailhead, south of the Salt Creek bridge -&gt; Start of the forest trail (SNO-3598 east end): straight (medium), 0.04 mi | 3. Start of the forest trail (SNO-3598 east end) -&gt; Forest trail meets the road (SNO-4378 start): usfs-trail (medium), 0.48 mi | 4. Forest trail meets the road (SNO-4378 start) -&gt; West end of the road part of the loop: usfs-trail (medium), 0.45 mi | 5. West end of the road part of the loop -&gt; Diamond Creek Falls trailhead (loop closed): usfs-trail (medium), 1.43 mi | 6. Diamond Creek Falls trailhead (loop closed) -&gt; Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park: usfs-trail (high), 0.17 mi</desc>
